 The bounded inherited-reference recovery also requires the live merged file to remain exactly the reviewed migration endpoint when it first materializes that old pin. Subsequent collection and certificate evidence carry only immutable history, so later ordinary deterministic merged-contract rebuilds do not need that initial endpoint to remain current. Saved source receipts retain their original bytes; they are never relabeled as current metadata review.
 
 The dependency-ledger merger authenticates the same exact PnP receipt before retaining a pre-migration item-edge finding as historical. It checks the current canonical consumer home but preserves every original row field and marks `current_review_credit:false`; it never copies that finding onto a current edge. Current declared edges are still collected from current manifests and sources. They require their own explicit current-ID findings wherever `--require-reviewed` applies. This is the existing original-slot history policy for the two explicitly authenticated run-local migrations, not alias-based ownership or new mathematical review credit.
+
+The centralized Step 5 guard distinguishes the authenticated current algorithm identity from a genuine new creation. Its comparison snapshot must omit the old identity and match the current centralized algorithm guard, and `licensedPnpReplacement` must still authenticate the receipt, fresh native algorithm/consumer reviews and current certification. Only that exact current ID bypasses the separate creation-record requirement, just as the independently authenticated OP-to-EX original slot does. Raw changed/created/deleted observations and all other creation/provenance checks remain unchanged.
